<article class="env-lemma" id="056N">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/056N">Lemma <span data-tag="056N">31.14.5</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme. Let $D \subset S$ be an effective Cartier divisor. Let $s \in D$. If $\dim _ s(S) < \infty $, then $\dim _ s(D) < \dim _ s(S)$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Assume $\dim _ s(S) < \infty $. Let $U = \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A) \subset S$ be an affine open neighbourhood of $s$ such that $\dim (U) = \dim _ s(S)$ and such that $D = V(f)$ for some nonzerodivisor $f \in A$ (see Lemma <a href="/tag/01WS" data-tag="01WS">31.14.2</a>). Recall that $\dim (U)$ is the Krull dimension of the ring $A$ and that $\dim (U \cap D)$ is the Krull dimension of the ring $A/(f)$. Then $f$ is not contained in any minimal prime of $A$. Hence any maximal chain of primes in $A/(f)$, viewed as a chain of primes in $A$, can be extended by adding a minimal prime. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>